# AI-BOS HTML Binding (sites/)

When working under `sites/`, treat the delivery project as **`PRJ-TMPL-HTML-001`**.

## Mandatory

1. Read `AI-BOS/project-registry/registry.json` entry `PRJ-TMPL-HTML-001` before material changes.
2. Load HTML domain pack: `HB-ENG-HTML-001`, `RU-AI-BOS-HTML-001`, `WF-DLV-HTML-SITE-001`.
3. Use `@html-website-builder` / `AG-DLV-HTML-LEAD-001` as lead; delegate subagents per skill.
3. Record evidence in `.cursor/execution/template-tasks.md`.

## Routing

| Need | Agent / skill |
|------|----------------|
| Lead build | `frontend-architect` / `@html-website-builder` (`AG-DLV-HTML-LEAD-001`) |
| Design tokens | `design-system-architect` (`AG-DLV-HTML-DS-001`) |
| Accessibility | `accessibility-auditor` (`AG-DLV-HTML-A11Y-001`) |
| Performance | `performance-optimizer` (`AG-DLV-HTML-PERF-001`) |
| Final QA | `code-reviewer` (`AG-DLV-HTML-QA-001`) |
| AI-BOS structural change | `@system-builder` |

## Never

- Introduce frameworks, CDN scripts, or build tools in `sites/` deliverables
- Skip readonly audit subagents at delivery
